        ("Procedure", "Before and after the four weeks, all students completed a 20-item questionnaire about their anxiety before tests. Each item was rated from 1 (never) to 5 (always), so scores could range from 20 to 100, with higher scores meaning more anxiety. Test anxiety was defined as a student's total score on the 20-item questionnaire."),
        ("Ethical procedures", "A college institutional review board approved the study. Students signed informed consent forms that described the course and the waiting list, and they were told they could stop at any time. Questionnaires were identified by code numbers, and counseling center information was given to every student."),
