        ("A survey of students and teachers", "Researchers surveyed 600 students and 120 teachers in six schools. Of the students, 58 percent said that they check their phones at least five times during a typical class, and 44 percent said that having their phone during class helps them feel less anxious. Of the teachers, 71 percent said that phones distract students during lessons. The researchers noted that participants who volunteered to answer the survey may feel more strongly about phones than others."),
